IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hprnl-dates`
IMPORT `hprnl-practitioner`

-- Health Practitioner Regulation National Law (Victoria) Act 2009 -- worked cases for the practitioner's questions
-- (hprnl-practitioner.l4) and the date helpers. Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none
-- was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the
-- law. The facts are illustrative.
-- Day counts used: 1 July 2012 + 28 days = 29 July 2012; 10 March 2026 + 28 = 7 April 2026 (21 days left in March, 7
-- into April); 20 December 2025 + 28 = 17 January 2026; 2028 is a leap year, so 1 February 2028 + 28 = 29 February 2028
-- and 31 January 2028 + 28 = 28 February 2028.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`tribunal matter` MEANS `a matter the National Law gives to the responsible tribunal`
`magistrate matter` MEANS `a matter the National Law gives to a magistrate or a magistrates' court`
`VCAT` MEANS `VCAT (the Victorian Civil and Administrative Tribunal), the responsible tribunal for Victoria (s 6)`
`Magistrates` MEANS `a magistrate within the meaning of the Magistrates' Court Act 1989, or the Magistrates' Court of Victoria (s 5)`
`no appeal` MEANS `not covered: s 6A gives me no appeal, because I am not the subject of an appellable decision under s 199 of the National Law`
`before the Law` MEANS `not covered: the National Law did not apply in Victoria before 1 July 2010 (s 2), so no appellable decision under it was made`
`before s 6A` MEANS `not covered: s 6A does not apply to an application lodged before 1 July 2012 (s 9(1)); its time limit is outside this Act`
`not begun` MEANS `yes, in time: I may apply to VCAT for review; the 28 days have not begun, because I have not yet been given notice of the decision (s 6A)`
`in time` MEANS `yes, in time: I may apply to VCAT for review, no more than 28 days after I was given notice of the decision (s 6A)`
`late` MEANS `no, out of time: more than 28 days after I was given notice of the decision (s 6A(2)); VCAT may extend the time (VCAT Act s 126)`
`in time s 9` MEANS `yes, in time: the decision was made before 1 July 2012, and I lodge no more than 28 days after 1 July 2012 (s 9(2))`
`late s 9` MEANS `no, out of time: the decision was made before 1 July 2012, and I lodge more than 28 days after 1 July 2012 (s 9(2)); VCAT may extend the time (VCAT Act s 126)`

§§ `Dates`

#ASSERT `the date` 28 `days after` (`d` 1 7 2012) EQUALS `d` 29 7 2012
#ASSERT `the date` 28 `days after` (`d` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `d` 7 4 2026
#ASSERT `the date` 28 `days after` (`d` 1 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 10 3 2026) `to` (`d` 7 4 2026) EQUALS 28
#ASSERT `the day` (`d` 30 6 2010) `is before` (`d` 1 7 2010)
#ASSERT NOT (`the day` (`d` 1 7 2010) `is before` (`d` 1 7 2010))

§§ `ss 6A(2), 9(2) -- the rule with its deadline`

-- Lodged on day 0, day 28 and day 29 counted from the day the 28 days run from (fork F1).
#ASSERT `lodged in time under` (`ss 6A(2), 9(2) -- lodge within the days allowed` 28) `at` 0
#ASSERT `lodged in time under` (`ss 6A(2), 9(2) -- lodge within the days allowed` 28) `at` 28
#ASSERT NOT (`lodged in time under` (`ss 6A(2), 9(2) -- lodge within the days allowed` 28) `at` 29)

§§ `ss 2, 4 -- the National Law as a law of Victoria`

#ASSERT `Does the National Law apply to me in Victoria` (`d` 1 7 2010) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the National Law apply to me in Victoria` (`d` 30 6 2010) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the National Law apply to me in Victoria` (`d` 7 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 5, 6 -- where my matter is heard`

#ASSERT `Where will my matter be heard` `tribunal matter` (`d` 7 11 2026) EQUALS `VCAT`
#ASSERT `Where will my matter be heard` `magistrate matter` (`d` 7 11 2026) EQUALS `Magistrates`
#ASSERT `Where will my matter be heard` `another matter` (`d` 7 11 2026) EQUALS `not covered: this Act names no court or tribunal for this matter`
#ASSERT `Where will my matter be heard` `tribunal matter` (`d` 1 7 2010) EQUALS `VCAT`
#ASSERT `Where will my matter be heard` `tribunal matter` (`d` 30 6 2010) EQUALS `not covered: the National Law did not apply in Victoria before 1 July 2010 (s 2)`
#ASSERT `Where will my matter be heard` `magistrate matter` (`d` 30 6 2010) EQUALS `not covered: the National Law did not apply in Victoria before 1 July 2010 (s 2)`

§§ `ss 6A, 9 -- can I apply to VCAT in time`

-- Not an appellable decision, or not about me: s 6A gives no appeal.
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` FALSE TRUE (`d` 2 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2026) (`d` 20 3 2026) EQUALS `no appeal`
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` TRUE FALSE (`d` 2 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2026) (`d` 20 3 2026) EQUALS `no appeal`
-- A decision dated before the National Law applied in Victoria.
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` TRUE TRUE (`d` 30 6 2010) TRUE (`d` 30 6 2010) (`d` 20 7 2012) EQUALS `before the Law`
-- s 9(1): lodged before 1 July 2012 is outside s 6A; on 1 July 2012 it is inside.
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2012) TRUE (`d` 5 3 2012) (`d` 30 6 2012) EQUALS `before s 6A`
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2012) TRUE (`d` 5 3 2012) (`d` 1 7 2012) EQUALS `in time s 9`
-- s 9(2): a decision made before 1 July 2012; the last day is 29 July 2012, whenever notice was given (fork F2).
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2012) TRUE (`d` 5 3 2012) (`d` 29 7 2012) EQUALS `in time s 9`
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2012) TRUE (`d` 5 3 2012) (`d` 30 7 2012) EQUALS `late s 9`
-- Decided and notified on 30 June 2012, lodged 29 July 2012: 29 days after notice, but s 9(2) governs, so in time.
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` TRUE TRUE (`d` 30 6 2012) TRUE (`d` 30 6 2012) (`d` 29 7 2012) EQUALS `in time s 9`
-- Decided 30 June 2012, no notice ever given, lodged 30 July 2012: s 9(2) still bars it (finding 2).
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` TRUE TRUE (`d` 30 6 2012) FALSE (`d` 30 6 2012) (`d` 30 7 2012) EQUALS `late s 9`
-- s 6A(2): a decision made on 1 July 2012, notice that day; day 28 and day 29.
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 7 2012) TRUE (`d` 1 7 2012) (`d` 29 7 2012) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 7 2012) TRUE (`d` 1 7 2012) (`d` 30 7 2012) EQUALS `late`
-- A refusal of registration on 2 March 2026, notice on 10 March 2026: the last day is 7 April 2026.
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` TRUE TRUE (`d` 2 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2026) (`d` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` TRUE TRUE (`d` 2 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2026) (`d` 7 4 2026) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` TRUE TRUE (`d` 2 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2026) (`d` 8 4 2026) EQUALS `late`
-- Across a year end: notice 20 December 2025, last day 17 January 2026.
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` TRUE TRUE (`d` 15 12 2025) TRUE (`d` 20 12 2025) (`d` 17 1 2026) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` TRUE TRUE (`d` 15 12 2025) TRUE (`d` 20 12 2025) (`d` 18 1 2026) EQUALS `late`
-- A leap year: notice 1 February 2028, last day 29 February 2028.
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2028) TRUE (`d` 1 2 2028) (`d` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `in time`
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2028) TRUE (`d` 1 2 2028) (`d` 1 3 2028) EQUALS `late`
-- No notice yet, or lodged before the day of notice: the 28 days have not begun (fork F3).
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` TRUE TRUE (`d` 2 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 1 9 2026) EQUALS `not begun`
#ASSERT `Can I apply to VCAT in time` TRUE TRUE (`d` 2 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2026) (`d` 9 3 2026) EQUALS `not begun`

§§ `ss 6A(2), 9(2) -- by when must I apply`

#ASSERT `By when must I apply to VCAT` TRUE TRUE (`d` 2 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (`d` 7 4 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to VCAT` TRUE TRUE (`d` 15 12 2025) TRUE (`d` 20 12 2025) EQUALS JUST (`d` 17 1 2026)
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to VCAT` TRUE TRUE (`d` 31 1 2028) TRUE (`d` 31 1 2028) EQUALS JUST (`d` 28 2 2028)
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to VCAT` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 2 2028) TRUE (`d` 1 2 2028) EQUALS JUST (`d` 29 2 2028)
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to VCAT` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 7 2012) TRUE (`d` 1 7 2012) EQUALS JUST (`d` 29 7 2012)
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to VCAT` TRUE TRUE (`d` 30 6 2012) TRUE (`d` 15 7 2012) EQUALS JUST (`d` 29 7 2012)
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to VCAT` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 3 2012) FALSE (`d` 1 3 2012) EQUALS JUST (`d` 29 7 2012)
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to VCAT` TRUE TRUE (`d` 2 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to VCAT` FALSE TRUE (`d` 2 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to VCAT` TRUE FALSE (`d` 2 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to VCAT` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 1 2010) TRUE (`d` 5 1 2010) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 7 -- Victorian Acts that do not apply`

#ASSERT `Does this Victorian Act apply to the National Law in Victoria` `the Audit Act 1994` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this Victorian Act apply to the National Law in Victoria` `the Financial Management Act 1994` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this Victorian Act apply to the National Law in Victoria` `the Freedom of Information Act 1982` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this Victorian Act apply to the National Law in Victoria` `the Health Records Act 2001` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this Victorian Act apply to the National Law in Victoria` `the Interpretation of Legislation Act 1984` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this Victorian Act apply to the National Law in Victoria` `the Ombudsman Act 1973` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this Victorian Act apply to the National Law in Victoria` `the Privacy and Data Protection Act 2014` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this Victorian Act apply to the National Law in Victoria` `the Public Administration Act 2004` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this Victorian Act apply to the National Law in Victoria` `the Subordinate Legislation Act 1994` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this Victorian Act apply to the National Law in Victoria` `another Victorian Act` EQUALS NOTHING
